# Keep the build context to what the image actually needs: the solution file and src/.
# Everything else is either irrelevant to the build or must never reach an image.

# Secrets first -- nothing resembling an env file may enter the context.
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# Build output (and anything built for the host architecture, which would be the wrong one).
**/bin/
**/obj/
artifacts/

# Not part of the published worker.
tests/
dev/
deploy/
docs/
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.claude/
*.md
!README.md
LICENSE

# Runtime state that only exists on a developer machine.
logs/
